---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy — Kindling" description="Kindling's Phase 0 privacy notice.">
  <article class="legal section-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Draft for validation</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-notice">Last updated August 12, 2026. This is a pre-launch draft and requires legal review before app-store release.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>The prototype keeps the task and suggested step in the current browser tab. They are not placed in analytics events or sent to Kindling. Anonymous interaction events are buffered in your browser for research export.</p>

    <h2>Waitlist email</h2>
    <p>If you join the waitlist, Formspark receives and stores your email address on Kindling's behalf so we can manage early-access invitations and occasional product updates. We do not ask Formspark to receive task text. You may ask to be removed from the waitlist or unsubscribe from any future marketing message.</p>

    <h2>Prototype events</h2>
    <p>The prototype records event names, timestamps, a random session identifier, and limited choices such as the session outcome. Events never contain the task or first-step text. By default they remain in local browser storage until you copy them for a research session or clear them.</p>

    <h2>Website analytics</h2>
    <p>The deployed website may use Vercel Web Analytics to measure aggregate visitors, page views, devices, and referrers. Vercel describes this analytics service as anonymous and cookie-free. Kindling does not place task or first-step text in page URLs or analytics properties.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can clear the prototype's event buffer from the Research mode panel. You can also clear site data through your browser. To request removal from the waitlist, reply to a Kindling email or use its unsubscribe link.</p>

    <h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Kindling is a productivity tool. It does not diagnose, monitor, or treat ADHD or any medical condition, and it is not a substitute for professional care.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
